  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the retail price of one pack of glue sticks at the school-supply store? Mr. Jackson’s fourth-grade class has 28 students.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. The class has 28 students, but this only tells us the number of students.\n2. No price, total cost, or number of glue-stick packs is provided.\n3. Therefore, the retail price of one pack cannot be determined from the given information.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined from the information given.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Mr. Jackson’s fourth-grade class has 27 students.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Even with 27 students, the number of students does not provide any information about the price of a pack of glue sticks. A cost or price relationship is still needed.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined from the information given.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the glue sticks come in packs of 9.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. There are 27 students.\n2. Each pack contains 9 glue sticks:\n\n\\[\n27 \\div 9 = 3\n\\]\n\nSo, the class would need 3 packs if each student gets one glue stick. However, no cost for the packs is given, so the retail price of one pack cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined from the information given.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. The glue sticks come in packs of 8.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With 27 students and 8 glue sticks per pack:\n\n\\[\n27 \\div 8 = 3\\text{ remainder }3\n\\]\n\nThus, the class would need 4 packs to give each student one glue stick. However, no price information is provided.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price of one pack cannot be determined.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the school-supply store sells each pack of glue sticks for $6.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The store sells each pack of glue sticks for **$6**. Therefore, the retail price of one pack is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: the store does not offer discounts on glue-stick packs.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the store charges **$6 per pack** and offers no discounts, the retail price of one pack remains:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many packs of glue sticks does Mr. Jackson need to buy so every student can have 2 glue sticks? By the way, here are some relevant details: Mr. Jackson wants to give each student 2 glue sticks. Mr. Jackson can only buy whole packs and expects to have some extra glue sticks left over.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Mr. Jackson needs \\(27 \\times 2 = 54\\) glue sticks.\n2. Each pack contains 8 glue sticks.\n3. Divide:\n\n\\[\n54 \\div 8 = 6\\text{ remainder }6\n\\]\n\nSince he can buy only whole packs, he must buy 7 packs:\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 8 = 56\n\\]\n\nThis provides 2 extra glue sticks.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7\\text{ packs}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
